body: |-
  FILES/LINES:
  - native.ts proposeNative (~394): meaning-NOOP is a TRUE no-op ONLY when baseStrand.binding.treeId === snap.treeId; otherwise fall through and seal (byte-custody strand: empty delta, stateId === parent's, binding.treeId moved).
  - native.ts admitNative NOOP branch (~674): when the scratch tip linearly fast-forwards the selvage (baseStrand.pickId === selvageTipId) and scratchTree !== selvageTree, advance the ref (writeRef/writeSelvage/clearScratch) and return status FAST_ADMIT sealed:true. A byte-only change under a CONCURRENT meaning advance (base ≠ selvage tip) is NOT a linear fast-forward and stays a NOOP — no silent carry across a divergence.
  - native.ts admitNative (~672): new closure persistContested(dec) — the buildKnotPayload+persistKnotPayload path, try/catch RETURNS {id?|error?} instead of swallowing.
  - native.ts downgrade site (~697): CLEAN-but-bytes-overlap now calls persistContested({...decision,status:'KNOT'}) and threads knotPayloadId + payloadError + the payload id into meaningRefusal.
  - native.ts KNOT/DANGLE site (~768): refactored to call the same persistContested helper (two sites cannot drift about what lands in the denominator).
  - admit.ts AdmitResult (~300): added optional payloadError?: string (G1-additive) — a lost work order must be visible, not byte-identical to a quiet repo.
  - strand.ts byteOnly doc (~214): corrected — it previously CLAIMED native "has no NOOP gap"; now documents the derived byte-custody behavior on both paths.

  TESTS: byte-custody-native.test.ts — (1) an asset-only (.txt, non-lens) edit proposes non-noop, admits FAST_ADMIT, and the bytes are canonical on a fresh restore while the meaning file is untouched; (2) a true no-op (no byte change after fork) still returns noop:true. Gotcha: restore() takes {to}, not {into}.

  NOT YET COVERED (follow-up): a deterministic test that reaches the byte-conflict DOWNGRADE and asserts the payload persisted + health counts it — constructing meaning-CLEAN + byte-conflict deterministically is fiddly (same-symbol edits read as a meaning KNOT, not a downgrade). Refactor-to-helper is covered by existing KNOT/DANGLE tests staying green; the downgrade-persist enhancement wants its own test in the tester pass.

  CONCURRENCY NOTE: two builder subagents were editing resolve.ts/knot-payload.ts (I-1) and oracle.ts/cli.ts (I-2/hazard) at the same time on disjoint files; full-suite run deferred until they land.
